+# Research Questions
+
+1. [codebase] How do the existing subagent dispatch sites across `skills/**/SKILL.md` and `agents/qrspi-*.md` currently express model choice (frontmatter, inline override, env var, or hardcoded default), and which surfaces are read at dispatch time vs. at session start?
+2. [web] How do open-source plugin and agent frameworks (Claude Code plugins, OpenDevin, AutoGen, LangGraph, Aider) express per-component model-routing policies in configuration, and what schema shapes (per-role defaults, per-task overrides, layered precedence) are common in their published configs?
+3. [codebase] What is the call shape, error handling, and stdout/stderr contract of `scripts/run-codex-review.sh` and `scripts/codex-companion-bg.sh`, and how does main chat or a dispatching skill consume their output?
+4. [web] What are the documented OpenAI Chat Completions compatibility surfaces, request/response shapes, streaming semantics, and error-code conventions for DeepSeek-V3 and Kimi K2 (Moonshot) endpoints as of 2026-05?
+5. [web] What patterns does the Medium article "I was burning through Claude Code's weekly limit in 3 days — here's how I fixed it" (https://medium.com/@kunalbhardwaj598/i-was-burning-through-claude-codes-weekly-limit-in-3-days-here-s-how-i-fixed-it-0344c555abda) describe for shell-side third-party LLM dispatch, session-state propagation, API-key handling, and error fallback?
+6. [codebase] How does `skills/plan/SKILL.md` currently structure its generation-side sub-subagent dispatch (input bounds, output contract, ID-hygiene expectations, status reporting), and where in the SKILL flow does the post-approval split-into-task-files step live today?
+7. [codebase] What are the canonical task-file templates under `templates/` or referenced by `skills/plan/SKILL.md` for `tasks/task-NN.md`, and what frontmatter/section contracts must any mechanical split preserve?
+8. [codebase] Which dispatch sites across `skills/` and `agents/` repeatedly include the same long stable files (SKILL bodies, reviewer-protocol, implementer-protocol) in prompt composition, and how is that composition currently assembled?
+9. [web] What prior art exists for prompt-context summarization shims or pre-computed file indices (line-range section maps) used as prompt inputs in agent frameworks, and how do those systems guard against summary drift becoming source-of-truth?
+10. [codebase] How does the TDD cycle inside `skills/implement/SKILL.md` and `agents/qrspi-implementer.md` currently sequence test-writing and production-code writing within a single dispatch, and where does `agents/qrspi-test-writer.md` already plug in (per `test-test-writer-tool-grant.bats`)?
+11. [web] What does published research and developer-tooling literature say about quality and failure-mode differences when test authoring is split from production-code authoring in LLM coding agents (shared context loss vs. separation of concerns)?
+12. [codebase] How does `skills/implementer-protocol/SKILL.md` thread reviewer finding IDs (`R<N>-F<NN>`), task IDs (`T<NN>`), and goal/question/design IDs into fix-cycle implementer prompts, and what existing guidance (if any) restricts those tokens from appearing in edited files?
+13. [codebase] What does `skills/parallelize/SKILL.md` mandate for Worktree-Aware Setup Validation in its process steps, and how does `skills/parallelize/owns-defers.md` currently partition responsibilities between Parallelize and Implement around worktree configuration vs. runtime worktree creation?
+14. [codebase] What Branch Map vocabulary (terms like `feature branch tip`, `task-NN tip`, `stage-after-W{N}`, `task-00 tip`, wave-suffix forms like `W4a/b/c`) is canonical in `skills/parallelize/SKILL.md` Branch Model and Worked Example, and where do `agents/qrspi-parallelize-reviewer.md` and `skills/reviewer-protocol/SKILL.md` define or contradict that vocabulary?
+15. [codebase] Where in the QRSPI pipeline (Plan, Parallelize, Implement, reviewer agents) do dispatch prompts treat a reference artifact (screenshot, golden file, fixture) as ground truth, and what gating, if any, validates the reference itself before downstream consumers fire?
+16. [codebase] What does `agents/qrspi-visual-fidelity-reviewer.md` (and the Keeplii reference noted in the user's memory at `~/.claude/projects/.../reference_keeplii_vfr_agent.md`) prescribe for handling explicit spec deltas vs. source-fidelity, and how do current lift-style task specs surface "drop this from source" instructions?
+17. [codebase] What is the exact ordering of scratch-file write, staging, and commit in the `skills/implementer-protocol/SKILL.md` commit procedure, and what does the qrspi-plus repo's `.gitignore` currently cover for transient implementer artifacts?
+18. [codebase] How does `tests/unit/test-u14-lint.bats` construct its file-path scan and excluded-skill substring check, and how do other BATS tests in `tests/unit/` derive skill identity from paths in a worktree-safe way?
+19. [codebase] What awk/grep section-extraction patterns recur across `tests/unit/test-skill-md-content-patterns.bats`, `test-cross-skill-contracts.bats`, and similar SKILL-body assertion tests, and what `REPO_ROOT`, empty-extract, and structural-anchor conventions do they share?
+20. [codebase] What boundary, if any, does `skills/replan/SKILL.md` currently draw between Replan's mechanical phase-snapshot work and the interactive scope-capture work owned by `skills/goals/SKILL.md`, and how does Replan today handle informal "Ideas" surfaced during a phase?
+21. [codebase] What is the current Branch Map and Execution Order presentation shape in `parallelization.md` artifacts (per `skills/parallelize/SKILL.md` Worked Example and any test fixtures under `tests/fixtures/`), and how do reviewer templates lint that shape?
+22. [web] What are the current GitHub Actions best-practice patterns (2025–2026) for running BATS test suites, installing `jq`/`yq`/`bats-core` on `ubuntu-latest`, and running ShellCheck across a `hooks/` tree, including matrix strategies and caching?
+23. [codebase] What branch-naming conventions are documented in `AGENTS.md`, `skills/implement/SKILL.md` Branch Model, and existing dispatch logic, and how do `qrspi/{slug}/...` and `{handle}/issue-{NNN}-{slug}` namespaces appear in current scripts or templates that would need to be reflected in CI trigger filters?
+24. [codebase] Which `skills/**/SKILL.md` and `agents/qrspi-*.md` files in the current `main` branch contain release-version tokens (e.g., `v0.6`, `v0.6.0`, `v0.7+`, `0.6+`) or milestone references, and what carve-outs exist today under `docs/qrspi/YYYY-MM-DD-*/` and version-tagged test files?
+25. [web] What lint/CI patterns do other markdown-driven prompt or skill libraries (Anthropic skills, Cursor rules, mdBook docs, evergreen-doc projects) use to detect and prevent release-version-token rot in evergreen contract files?
